From 98339c2fd65c9f2c6338b2dcdfb1df5ac835b3cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 20:20:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] =?UTF-8?q?fix(creatives):=20Meta=20removed=20=3Fids?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=3D=20in=20v26.0=20=E2=80=94=20creative=20hydration=20has=20bee?=
 =?UTF-8?q?n=20dead=20since=20late=20July?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase-2 creative hydration used Meta's multi-read endpoint,
GET /?ids=<id,id,…>&fields=<…>. Meta removed the `ids` query parameter
in Graph API v26.0, so every batch came back with

  meta_code=100 "The ids query parameter is deprecated in v26.0+."

fetchCreativeBatch swallows per-batch failures by design (a degraded
batch beats a dropped event), so this surfaced nowhere: hydration
returned an empty map on every event and every ad kept its phase-1
nulls. Cron logs show `creative_batch_done hydrated=0 missing=44` on
every event since.

Two visible symptoms, one dead transport:

  - Top Creatives tiles render initials placeholders instead of
    previews, because no image_url / video_id / thumbnail_url ever
    reaches the grouper.
  - The AI auto-tagger skips every creative for want of a thumbnail.
    creative_tag_assignments has not been written since 2026-07-28.

Swaps the transport to Meta's Batch API (POST / with a `batch` array),
the documented replacement. Same per-call ID budget, so
CREATIVE_BATCH_SIZE chunking is unchanged. The batch response is an
array of {code, body} where body is a JSON *string* and a sub-request
can fail inside a 200 envelope, so the parser rejects error envelopes
and id-less bodies rather than letting them land in the map as
creatives with every field undefined.

graphPostWithToken has no built-in retry unlike the graphGetWithToken
this used to go through, so the transient-retry posture is restored
explicitly rather than silently dropped along with the old transport.

Also in this change, both discovered while tracing the same symptom:

  - The cron 504s. It walks 131 eligible events sequentially at ~4 Meta
    round trips each, far past maxDuration=800. Every invocation was
    killed with no response body, no health signal, and no staleness
    alarm — active_creatives_snapshots looked fresh because manual
    dashboard refreshes kept writing to it. Adds a 600s wall-clock
    budget plus least-recently-refreshed ordering, so a capped run
    drains the stalest slice and consecutive runs rotate through the
    whole set instead of re-doing the head forever. eventsSkippedTimeBudget
    is reported on the response — a silently truncated run reading
    identically to a complete one is how this went unnoticed for three
    weeks.
  - The two live venue-creatives routes that feed the Top Creatives
    strip never passed enrichVideoThumbnails, so even once hydration
    works they would serve Meta's 64x64 asset-feed posters. Both already
    hold a service-role client; the helper is Storage-cache-first, so on
    the warm path this is one Storage read per video and zero Meta calls.

Tests: 14 new, covering the batch request builder (including a guard
against reverting to ids=), the sub-response parser's rejection
branches, and the rotation invariant that a drained slice moves to the
back. Typecheck clean on all changed files.

