From 29a72e5ab9f46f0836ba866f28867e4bfe437f5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 21:46:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(meta): migrate every remaining ?ids= caller off the
 endpoint Meta removed in v26.0
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The creative-hydration fix in the previous commit was one of EIGHT call
sites using `GET /?ids=<csv>&fields=<…>`. Meta removed the `ids` query
parameter in Graph API v26.0 (released 29 July 2026), so all eight have
been failing with meta_code=100 since 28-29 July. Every one of them
wraps the call in a try/catch that degrades to "no data" — correct for
one bad batch, catastrophic when every batch fails — so none of it
surfaced anywhere.

Confirmed dead, beyond creative hydration:

  - lib/audiences/sources.ts — page enrichment and video hydration for
    the audience builder. `audience_source_cache` last wrote 2026-07-27.
  - lib/budget-pacing/spend-fetch.ts — the hourly budget-pacing cron's
    lifetime-spend read on its >20-campaign path. Spend read as £0, so
    no 25/50/60/70/80/90/100% Slack alert has fired since. Alerts that
    never fire look exactly like alerts with nothing to say.
  - lib/meta/client.ts — ad-set dynamic-creative guards and custom
    audience availability. Both degrade to "unknown", which callers
    treat as permissive.
  - lib/reporting/event-insights.ts — campaign effective_status lookup.
  - app/api/meta/pages/enrich/route.ts — page enrichment, raw fetch.

Adds lib/meta/graph-multi-get{,-parse}.ts. `graphMultiGetByIds` is
signature-compatible with `graphGetWithToken` — same (path, params,
token), same `Record<string, T>` return — so seven of the eight sites
migrate by changing one identifier and no surrounding "look up res[id],
treat missing as unknown" logic needed re-reasoning about. Batch API
under the hood; sub-request failures are filtered rather than keyed, so
a `{error:{…}}` riding inside the batch's HTTP 200 can't masquerade as
a node with every field undefined.

Two sites needed more than an identifier swap:

  - spend-fetch.ts multiplexes two call shapes through one injected
    fetcher: a real GET on /{id}/insights (≤20 campaigns) and the
    multi-node read (>20). Only the second is affected, so
    fetchCampaignSpendPence takes an optional second fetcher,
    defaulting to the first for existing callers and tests.
  - pages/enrich builds its URL by hand and needed the POST envelope
    plus an array-vs-error-object narrowing on the response.

Field lists are now percent-encoded. Not cosmetic: budget pacing sends
`insights.date_preset(maximum){spend}` and the ad-set guard sends
`ads.limit(0).summary(true)`. Braces and parens are not legal raw in a
URL and `relative_url` is parsed as path+query, so unencoded they risk
a truncated field list — silently, in the same way as everything else
here.

Folds the previous commit's creative-batch-response.ts into the shared
module so there is one home for this, not two.

Tests: 20, replacing the 8 from the previous commit — including the
percent-encoding of both real-world field-expansion strings, the
error-envelope rejection, id-keyed collection, and a guard against
anyone reverting to ids=. Full lib suite: 51 failures before and after,
all pre-existing. Typecheck clean on all changed files.

Not fixed here, flagged: META_API_VERSION is unset, so lib/meta/client.ts
defaults to v21.0, which expires 21 January 2027. The `ids=` removal was
not gated on the version in the request URL — these calls failed on
v21.0 regardless — so pinning would not have prevented this. It is still
worth pinning to a supported version deliberately rather than finding
out at expiry.

